Schema validation happens before record processing
DLQ is NOT universal error handling
Connector RUNNING ≠ pipeline healthy

“The JDBC Sink appeared to work with record_key initially because inserts never exercised UPSERT logic. Once updates flowed, the sink required a primary key, but the Kafka key was empty since Debezium keeps the PK in the value. Switching to record_value allowed the sink to correctly resolve the primary key and perform UPSERTs.”

🧠 One-line rule to remember

Always add columns to sink first or immediately after source, and never rely on auto.evolve in production

Adding columns requires coordination; dropping columns is safe but leaves cleanup work in the sink.


Debezium produces change events, but the sink connector defines how those changes are interpreted, applied, filtered, or rejected.